  "notes": [
    "vs.py gives no light type codes. GAPS.tsv names 0 directional and 2 spot. spatial.light.point assumes 2 is a point light. This case creates types 0, 1 and 2. The source census reads the stored kind of each kLightNode (td81), so the live run settles the codes for both cases.",
    "Each light has a pan and tilt, so a directional or spot light stores a direction.",
    "In the probe of 2026-10-19, vs.SetSpreadAngle changed only the light of kind 2, so kind 2 is the spot light. Kinds 0, 1 and 3 kept spread angle 0. spatial.light.point passes kind 2, so its stored light is a spot light.",
    "The FBX export of the source of 2026-10-19 names each light. Kind 0 exports as Infinite_Light with LightType 1, directional. Kind 1 exports as Omni_Light with no LightType, which is 0, point. Kind 2 exports as Spot_Light with LightType 2, spot, OuterAngle 60 and InnerAngle 30. FBX also adds Ambient_Omni_Light for the document ambient light, which has no source object. The glTF export wrote no file for this document, which holds only lights."
  ]
